ACS FIREWALL CHANGE REQUEST - Pod{{ pod_id_padded }}
====================================================

CHANGE ID:    CHG-{{ prefix }}-2026-0552
REQUESTED BY: ACS Network Security
TARGET:       POD{{ pod_id_padded }}-SRV host firewall (Windows Defender
              Firewall on this server only)

FINDING
-------
The host firewall on POD{{ pod_id_padded }}-SRV contains a permissive inbound
rule:

    {{ prefix }}-CYDEPLOY-ALLOW-ANY-INBOUND

It accepts TCP traffic on any port from any source address - a troubleshooting
rule that was never removed. ACS Network Security has requested that it be
replaced with rules that permit only the communication this server actually
needs.

THE TRAP
--------
Tightening a firewall without knowing what depends on it breaks production. The
point of this lab is to let discovered system and dependency information drive
the network change.

REQUIRED SEQUENCE
-----------------
1. Review {{ prefix }}_Required_Communication_Matrix.csv.
2. Run CyDeploy discovery for Pod{{ pod_id_padded }} and identify which inbound
   paths the discovered systems and services appear to need.
3. Record your dependency analysis on {{ prefix }}_Dependency_Worksheet.docx.
4. Apply the approved change on this server: remove or disable the permissive
   rule, and create replacement rules named {{ prefix }}-CYDEPLOY-<purpose> that
   permit only the required paths. Each replacement rule must name specific
   remote addresses and specific ports - never "Any".
5. Validate that required connectivity still works after the change. Your own
   remote desktop session and the grading channel both depend on it.
6. Record the outcome on {{ prefix }}_Change_Validation_Report.docx and submit
   the response file described in your lab guide.

Scope: the local firewall of POD{{ pod_id_padded }}-SRV only. Do not change the
pod gateway, another pod, the shared domain, the campus firewall, or the
management network.
